Package: wsynthdid
Title: Synthetic Difference-in-Difference Estimation with Weighted Extensions
Version: 0.1.1
Author: Dmitry Arkhangelsky [aut]
        Susan Athey [aut]
        David A. Hirshberg [aut, cre]
        Guido W. Imbens [aut]
        Stefan Wager [aut]
        John Iselin [ctb]
        Erica Ryan [ctb]
Maintainer: David A. Hirshberg <david.a.hirshberg@gmail.com>
Description: Estimate average treatment effects in panel data using synthetic
    difference-in-differences. Extends the base SDID estimator of Arkhangelsky
    et al. (2021) with user-specified weights on treated units and post-treatment
    periods, enabling population-weighted or policy-relevant averaging. Includes
    weighted variants of the bootstrap, jackknife, and placebo variance estimators,
    as well as event-study decomposition. Supports both simultaneous adoption and
    staggered adoption (cohort-wise weighted estimation against not-yet-treated or
    never-treated controls, aggregated with researcher-chosen cohort weights).
Depends:
    R (>= 3.4)
Imports:
    methods,
    mvtnorm
